== Further Details ==
Start the quest by speaking with Juliette.

[[File:Gold Mine (Savanna Woodland).png|thumb|Gold Mine]]
'''At Quest {{Green|Step 1}}''', Romero can first be found behind and below {{NPCSprite|Master Tactician Funk}} in a cave at the {{zone|Savanna Woodland}}. Upon interacting with him, he asks you to get him {{Item|Yellow Rock|amount=1}}, which can be found by mining the gold ore in one of the savanna caves (do not use a {{EnchantmentsLink|Silk Touch}} pickaxe). Once obtained, he will pass you a {{Item|Poorly Wrapped Rock}}, which you must then pass to Juliette.

'''At Quest {{Green|Step 2}}''', Romero can be found at the {{zone|Village}}, near {{NPCSprite|Marco}}'s hut. He then asks you to obtain {{Item|Poppy|amount=16}} for him. Upon obtaining them, interacting with Romero will give you a {{Item|Rose Bouquet}}, which you also need to pass to Juliette.

[[File:Emerald Altar.png|thumb|The Emerald Altar]]
'''At Quest {{Green|Step 3}}''', Romero can be found at the Emerald Altar in the {{zone|Graveyard}}, to the left. He then needs you to pass him {{Item|Emerald|amount=64}}. Once you pass them to him, he will return a {{Item|Fake Emerald Altar}} which you questionably pass to Juliette.

'''At Quest {{Green|Step 4}}''', Romero can be found in the {{zone|Crimson Isle}}, in one of the underground {{Item|Nether Wart}} farms. He will require an {{Item|Enchanted Red Mushroom Block}}, which consists of {{Item|Red Mushroom|amount=25600}}.

'''At Quest {{Green|Step 5}}''', Romero is found at the wooden platform on top of the Mountain. He complains about the cold and asks for a Rabbit VI potion (Splash [[Potions]] does not work) brewed with Coffee, purchased from the [[Bartender]]. To brew the potion, you need an [[Enchanted Rabbit Foot]] and an [[Enchanted Glowstone]] (Or an [[Enchanted Redstone Lamp]]).

'''At Quest {{Green|Step 6}}''', Romero is found in the {{zone|Gold Mine}} next to a campfire. He is straight down and steep to the left. He will ask for an {{Item|Enchanted Lava Bucket}}.

[[File:Romero Treehouse.png|thumb|Romero's treehouse]]
'''At Quest {{Green|Step 7}}''', Romero is found at the house with a red and white roof in the {{zone|Wilderness}}, close to the [[Dark Auction]]. He asks for at least {{Stat|Intelligence|1,291}}. Note that this means a max {{stat|Mana}} of {{Green|1,391}}. 

Items to be considered:
*{{Item|Aurora Armor}}, which has quite high {{stat|int}} stat for its price.
*{{Item|Ender Monocle}}, extremely cheap power stone providing great {{stat|int}}.
*{{Item|Crystal Armor}} or {{Item|Bat Person Armor}} which can have doubled or tripled stats under certain conditions. This can be combined with the {{ReforgingLink|Wise}} or {{ReforgeLink|Necrotic}} reforges (the latter gives more {{stat|int}}).
**Crystal Armour can receive up to a 15 (187.5%) bonus by jumping next to the torch inside of the hut.
*{{Item|Bottle of Jyrre}}
*Held items that give {{stat|Int}}, such as {{Item|Dreadlord Sword}}, {{Item|Bonzo's Staff}}, or the more expensive {{Item|Spirit Sceptre}}, reforged to {{reforgelink|Heroic}}.

'''At Quest {{Green|Step 8}}''', Romero appears on the right side of the {{zone|Colosseum}} beside the smaller pool of water to the right of the entrance, where he asks for an {{Item|Emerald Blade}}.

[[File:Mushroom Desert Romero Hut Infographic.png|thumb|The location and appearance of Romero's desert hut]]
'''At Quest {{Green|Step 9}}''', Romero appears in a small house in the {{zone|Mushroom Desert}} at {{Coordinates|297|87|-562}}. He asks for a {{Item|Flower Minion}} from the [[Dark Auction]]. This is often the most expensive part of the quest, due to the high demand for Flower Minions.

'''At Quest {{Green|Step 10}}''', you need to get a tuxedo from {{NPCSprite|Taylor}}'s basement, costing 3 million to 75 million coins. Note that the tuxedo is ''not'' consumed by the quest. At this point, your {{Epic}} talisman will become {{Legendary}}. You also unlock the "Friar Lawrence" [[Achievement]].

Completing this whole quest can cost approximately {{c|50,000,000}} or more. It can vary depending on the price of a Flower Minion.

